sequenceDiagram
    %% Client input -> IRC command + local echo. IRC servers never echo back,
    %% so the echo is written locally or the message is invisible to clients.
    autonumber
    participant C as Client (web / apple / tui)
    participant WS as api/ws.go
    participant Parse as api/input.go parseInput
    participant Ctl as control.db
    participant Mgr as irc.Manager
    participant Srv as IRC server
    participant Log as network log DB
    participant Hub as hub.Hub
    participant PQ as preview queue

    C->>WS: {"type":"input","buffer_id":...,"content":"/me waves"}
    WS->>Ctl: LookupBuffer(buffer_id) -> networkID, name, kind
    WS->>Parse: parseInput(content, buffer)
    Parse-->>WS: clientCmd{type: "me", ...} (internal = true)
    opt command not in commandsAllowedForNonIRC
        WS->>Ctl: GetNetwork(networkID)
        alt kind is a non-IRC network (e.g. bluesky)
            WS-->>C: {"type":"error","msg":"command not supported on bluesky networks"}
        end
    end
    WS->>WS: handleCmd dispatch (cmdSend / cmdMe / cmdJoin / cmdMode / ...)

    Note over WS,Mgr: Plain text takes the cmdSend path below.
    C->>WS: {"type":"send","buffer_id":...,"content":"hello"}
    WS->>Ctl: LookupBuffer -> networkID, name, kind
    alt kind = status
        WS-->>C: error "cannot send to status buffer"
    end
    WS->>Mgr: Send(networkID, name, content)
    Mgr->>Srv: PRIVMSG name :hello
    Note over Srv: The server does NOT echo this back.
    WS->>Mgr: LogOutbound(ctx, networkID, name, "privmsg", content)
    Mgr->>Ctl: EnsureBuffer(networkID, target, channel|query)
    Mgr->>Log: InsertLogMessage(sender = own nick, kind, content)
    Log-->>Mgr: id, ts, inserted
    opt inserted
        Mgr->>Hub: Publish MessageEvent (WithSemantics -> is_self = true)
        Hub->>WS: fan-out to every subscriber, including the sender's own socket
        WS->>C: {"type":"message",...} - this is the echo the UI renders
        opt kind is privmsg / notice / action
            Mgr->>PQ: Enqueue(networkID, bufID, id, content)
        end
    end
    WS-->>C: {"type":"ack","req_id":...}
